   "name": "Mathematical Symbols",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Mathematical symbols"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What mathematical symbols do I need to know?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Starting with the basic four operations\n\n  - $+$  **Addition,** plus, sum, total\n  - $-$  **Subtraction,** minus, difference, take away\n  - $\\times$ **Multiplication,** product, times\n  - $\\div$ **Division,** quotient, divide, share"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Equals** signs\n\n  - $=$ Equal to\n  \n    - e.g.  $3x+7=19$\n  - $\\neq$ Not equal to\n  \n    - e.g.  $2-5\\neq5-2$\n  - $\\approx$ Approximately equal to\n  \n    - e.g.  $π\\approx3.14$\n  - $\\equiv$ Identical (equivalent) to\n  \n    - e.g.  $12x+6\\equiv3(4x+2)$"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Inequality** signs\n\n  - $>$ **Greater** than\n  \n    - e.g.  $5>-2$\n  - $<$ **Less** than\n  \n    - e.g.  $\\frac{1}{2}<\\frac{2}{3}$\n  - `greater-than or slanted equal to` Greater than or equal to\n  - `less-than or slanted equal to` Less than or equal to"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Other helpful symbols\n\n  - $()$  **Brackets**\n  \n    - used to group symbols\n    - e.g.  $(2x+4)--3(x+7)$\n  - $3^{x}$  **Powers** (also called indices, orders, or exponents)\n  \n    - repeated multiplication\n    - e.g.  $3^{4}=3\\times3\\times3\\times3=81$\n  - $\\sqrt{}$  **Positive square root**\n  \n    - inverse of squaring\n    - e.g.  $\\sqrt{81}=9$ because  $9^{2}=81$\n  - `cube root of blank`  **Cube root**\n  \n    - inverse of cubing\n    - e.g.  `cube root of 64 equals 4` because  $4^{3}=64$\n  - $\\pm$  **Plus Minus**\n  \n    - used to allow for both a positive and negative answer (two distinct answers)\n    - $a\\pmb$ is the same as $a+b$ and $a-b$\n    - e.g.  $x=3\\pm2.5$ is the same as $x=3+2.5=5.5$ and $x=3-2.5=0.5$\n  - $π$  **Pi**\n  \n    - the ratio of the circumference of a circle to its diameter"
  }
 ]
